WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 005, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.807
<v The Grandson>This cross is about a thousand years old.

2
00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:06.085
<v The Grandson>Who carved it,
and whose name does it keep?

3
00:00:10.505 --> 00:00:14.014
<v the monk of Llandough>[in Welsh] Bore da.
Mind the mud by the cross.

4
00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:18.734
<v the monk of Llandough>The masons cut it from pale stone
fetched from Sutton, down the Vale,

5
00:00:18.854 --> 00:00:21.310
<v the monk of Llandough>and set it here by Dochdwy's church,

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.939
<v the monk of Llandough>where every soul going
in to pray must pass it.

7
00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.559
<v The Grandson>It still stands.
A pillar-cross of Sutton stone,

8
00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:32.012
<v The Grandson>carved some time in the
tenth or eleventh century.

9
00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.886
<v The Grandson>Nobody can pin the year.

10
00:00:34.306 --> 00:00:36.773
<v the monk of Llandough>The letters on the shaft read IRBICI.

11
00:00:36.893 --> 00:00:40.160
<v the monk of Llandough>I trace them for the boys
learning their letters.

12
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.438
<v the monk of Llandough>Whose name it keeps,
the stone does not tell.

13
00:00:43.858 --> 00:00:45.724
<v the monk of Llandough>Now word comes from Cardiff.

14
00:00:45.844 --> 00:00:50.111
<v the monk of Llandough>The Norman lord Fitzhamon has
given lands, this hill among them,

15
00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:52.031
<v the monk of Llandough>to the abbey at Tewkesbury,

16
00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:57.765
<v the monk of Llandough>and the prior of St Mary's in Cardiff
is to be our lord of the manor.

17
00:00:58.185 --> 00:01:01.118
<v The Grandson>That 1106 grant reaches
us through one page:

18
00:01:01.238 --> 00:01:06.501
<v The Grandson>a letter printed in the Penarth Times
in 2011, on the history of St Mary's.

19
00:01:06.921 --> 00:01:09.728
<v The Grandson>A letter to a newspaper isn't the charter.

20
00:01:09.848 --> 00:01:12.848
<v The Grandson>It names Fitzhamon,
Tewkesbury and the prior,

21
00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:15.435
<v The Grandson>but we haven't seen the grant itself,

22
00:01:15.555 --> 00:01:18.713
<v The Grandson>and it doesn't show which
fields went with it.

23
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:24.066
<v the monk of Llandough>Abbey or prior, the hay still wants
cutting. Lords change; the hill stays.

24
00:01:24.486 --> 00:01:28.697
<v the monk of Llandough>Every spring we walk the bounds,
stone to stone, cwm to cwm,

25
00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:30.922
<v the monk of Llandough>and a clerk writes them down.

26
00:01:31.342 --> 00:01:34.851
<v The Grandson>And a clerk in 1392 may
have done just that.

27
00:01:34.971 --> 00:01:37.371
<v The Grandson>The Grandson's folders hold a family

28
00:01:37.491 --> 00:01:40.358
<v The Grandson>research note pointing
to Cwm-Cedwyn in the

29
00:01:40.478 --> 00:01:43.144
<v The Grandson>Llandough boundary records of that year.

30
00:01:43.564 --> 00:01:46.164
<v The Grandson>But plainly: we don't hold that record.

31
00:01:46.284 --> 00:01:48.551
<v The Grandson>Nobody here has seen the original,

32
00:01:48.671 --> 00:01:53.232
<v The Grandson>so the note doesn't show the 1392
record exists or what it holds,

33
00:01:53.352 --> 00:01:56.159
<v The Grandson>and it isn't proof of a Cedwyn Estate.

34
00:01:56.279 --> 00:01:58.034
<v The Grandson>It's a name to chase.

35
00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:03.654
<v The Grandson>The cross entry comes from a local-history
blog, sconzani, on the Irbic cross.

36
00:02:03.774 --> 00:02:07.774
<v The Grandson>A good modern write-up;
I'd still like the survey behind it.

37
00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.994
<v the monk of Llandough>Write it down, whoever you are.
Stone outlasts parchment.

38
00:02:12.414 --> 00:02:14.870
<v The Grandson>Next, the leases. Paper we can hold.
